* Behavioral optocoupler models for digital twin.
* The LED (input) side is a real diode. The output side is a behavioral
* current source that turns on when the LED is forward-biased above ~1V.

* PC817 - general purpose optocoupler (SMD-4)
* Pinout: 1=Anode, 2=Cathode, 3=Emitter, 4=Collector
.SUBCKT PC817 A K C E
D_LED A K LEDMOD
R_off C E 1Meg
B_photo C E I = { (V(A,K) > 1.0) ? V(C,E)/100 : 0 }
.ENDS

* 6N137 - high speed optocoupler (SMD-8)
* Pinout: 2=Anode, 3=Cathode, 5=GND, 6=VO
.SUBCKT 6N137 A K VO GND
D_LED A K LEDMOD
R_off VO GND 1Meg
B_photo VO GND I = { (V(A,K) > 1.0) ? V(VO,GND)/100 : 0 }
.ENDS